<title>UK: NWE jet strengthens in line with futures.</title>
<headline>NWE jet strengthens in line with futures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel rose on Monday as benchmark IPE gas oil futures were pulled higher by strengthening crude markets, traders said.</p>
<p>July IPE gas oil closed $1.50 higher at $165.25 a tonne.</p>
<p>Jet fuel barge premiums (fob ARA) were steady around July IPE +$15.00/+$16.00 fob ARA while cargo premiums (cif NWE) were steady to a shade firmer at +$17.50/+$18.00 a tonne, traders said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
